# Copy to legacy-redirect.caddy (git-ignored) on the server and restart caddy (dc up -d caddy).
# Every request to the old name or to www is answered with a permanent redirect to the real domain,
# so old links, bookmarks and search results keep working and search engines move their ranking across.
#
# The http:// names are listed explicitly: without them Caddy first answers plain-http requests with its
# own 308 hop to https://, and Google's "Change of address" check insists on a 301 directly from the old
# homepage. Listing both schemes makes every variant a single 301.
http://sharpen-ai.duckdns.org, https://sharpen-ai.duckdns.org, http://www.sharpenscore.com, https://www.sharpenscore.com {
    redir https://sharpenscore.com{uri} permanent
}
